            "data": "",
            "alt": "Refer to caption",
            "desc": "Figure 1: Illustration of the Taylor expansion framework for analyzing LA methods, highlighting the potential for more flexible attribution design. While independent effects can be allocated in a targeted manner, interaction effects call for more nuanced consideration, particularly in model-agnostic settings with limited prior knowledge. Many well-recognized methods still rely on fixed, predefined allocations, e.g., SHAP adopts a uniform distribution among the features involved.",
